        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> When the parameter label returned by the language server is a substring of the function name, that part of the function name will be highlighted instead of the parameter.\n> \n> In the attached screenshot you can see the signature help from mini.completion and the nvim built-in version that works as expected. Looking at the code, the built in one searches for string matches starting from the first trigger character instead of from the beginning of the signature.\n\nYes, indeed, this is the behavior of both of them. The Neovim behavior was added in neovim/neovim#15032 and the PR itself has questions about whether using trigger characters to detect function signature start is a good idea. The 'mini.completion' behavior is according to the LSP specification, as there is no indication that trigger characters are a reliable source of the \"start of function signature\".\n\nThis relies on LSP server advertising its capabilities with `signatureHelpProvider.triggerCharacters` containing start of function signature (usually `(` character, but I assume a space for `fennel-ls`). In practice they indeed usually do, but that is not according to the LSP spec while deviating from it can bring issues for some other servers. So for such cases I (and more recent than 2021 Neovim core, for that matter) usually tend to go \"better follow LSP spec\" route.\n\nSo all in all, I am going to close this as a know behavior. For LSP server to not have these kind of issues, it can return label start-end offsets (which 'mini.completion' supports).\n\n---\n\n> Also, a small thing you can see in my screenshot: maybe the highlight group should link to `LspSignatureActiveParameter` by default?\n\nThe `MiniCompletionActiveParameter` highlight group of 'mini.completion' was introduced (2021-10-13 on initial release) before `LspSignatureActiveParameter` was added to the stable version of Neovim (Neovim=0.6.0 on 2021-11-30). But it is indeed *might* be worth the change now, especially with the currently ongoing overhaul of 'mini.completion'. That is a different issue and I'll look into it.",
            "created_at": "2025-04-04T12:28:15Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1725#issuecomment-2778580490",
